  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "new_object",
    "file": "libredwg/src/in_dxf.c",
    "description": "`new_object` mishandles a DXF group-code 310 common-entity `preview` field for PLANESURFACE/SURFACE when the active subclass is not exactly `AcDbEntity`. The specialized `add_ent_preview` path is skipped, and the generic DynAPI assignment shallow-copies `pair->value.s` into `obj->tio.entity->preview`. The `Dxf_Pair` still owns that allocation. On the later `invalid_dxf` path, `dxf_free_pair` frees the string, leaving `entity->preview` dangling; cleanup then frees it again in `dwg_free_common_entity_data`. The fix should ensure such preview data is decoded/copied into independently owned storage (preferably route code 310 through `add_ent_preview` for surface subclasses), rather than suppressing either free.",
    "conditions": "A malformed ASCII DXF is parsed through `dwg_read_dxf`, reaches the BLOCKS section, and creates a SURFACE entity resolved as PLANESURFACE. It supplies a group-code 310 string/binary preview while the current subclass is a surface subclass rather than exactly `AcDbEntity`, causing the generic common-field assignment to alias the pair's allocated string. A subsequent invalid DXF code makes `new_object` take `invalid_dxf` and free that pair; `dwg_read_dxf` returns a critical error and the harness calls `dwg_free`, which frees the dangling PLANESURFACE preview a second time."
  },
